WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.260
Samsung plans fivefold Shion v9 nan growth, to 50,000 wafers for AI SSDs. This is AI Chips &amp; Data Centres, Episode 65. Memory

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:16.140
revenue cuts, a phoenix power contract, and a fresh push on chip export rules come after that. Then

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:22.260
what's on the horizon? Samsung tech power up reports from sole economic daily and industry sources

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:28.340
is converting NAND inside the second Shion fab rather than building a new one. The X2 line

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:35.980
now runs about 10,300 millimeter wafers a month of 286 layer V9, and the extra output is

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:41.560
aimed at enterprise drives for AI data centers. An electroplating line would fill empty clean room

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:47.740
space, equipment would move in around February 2027, and the conversion would finish that November.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:55.180
20-30% of the existing V6 line would switch to V9 as well. Samsung has previously denied that

00:00:55.180 --> 00:01:00.080
it was expanding production capacity, so this reads as a reshuffle even while the wafer

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.780
count jumps, and NAND's spot prices have already started falling.

00:01:04.741 --> 00:01:09.721
Trend Force in a separate tech power-up report says Chinese cloud service providers have

00:01:09.721 --> 00:01:14.521
cut their 2027 memory orders, and that cut is pressing the price outlook down.

00:01:15.221 --> 00:01:20.581
NAND Flash is expected to enter a downward pricing cycle as supply keeps expanding, and

00:01:20.581 --> 00:01:25.601
And the 2027 NAND revenue forecast is now about $419.3 billion.

00:01:26.521 --> 00:01:31.761
DRAM is still expected to stay short of demand, but the quarterly price increases are projected

00:01:31.761 --> 00:01:32.261
to ease.

00:01:32.881 --> 00:01:37.221
The DRAM revenue forecast for that year comes down to $1.15 trillion.

00:01:38.001 --> 00:01:42.624
Intel Biggo Finance Reports has won a Microsoft Packaging Order.

00:01:43.224 --> 00:01:49.184
Core Weave says robotics data is 3D scenes and sensor streams, and one physical AI program

00:01:49.184 --> 00:01:52.964
can generate petabytes of it because training reads the set again and again.

00:01:53.604 --> 00:01:57.964
Its local object transport accelerator caches that data on GPU nodes

00:01:57.964 --> 00:02:00.604
add up to seven gigabytes per second per GPU,

00:02:01.204 --> 00:02:03.904
so the processors train instead of waiting on the read.

00:02:04.584 --> 00:02:07.404
The post says those pieces then have to run as one loop.

00:02:08.666 --> 00:02:12.606
TSMC's North Phoenix campus is under construction toward a utility load

00:02:12.606 --> 00:02:16.266
of about 1.88 gigawatts, KBTX reports,

00:02:16.266 --> 00:02:19.906
and the first fab has been in production since late 2024.

00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:24.986
Arizona Public Service signed a direct pricing contract on October 16th

00:02:24.986 --> 00:02:28.466
to ramp service to that level for the fabs and advance packaging

00:02:28.466 --> 00:02:31.066
on an initial term of 25 years.

00:02:31.546 --> 00:02:36.706
Engineers at the Water Resource Center put campus use at 4.75 million gallons a day,

00:02:37.146 --> 00:02:41.986
mostly reclaimed wastewater plus a little ground water, all delivered by the City of Phoenix.

00:02:42.646 --> 00:02:48.706
TSMC says it recycles 65% of what it takes in, about 3.5 million gallons a day.

00:02:49.086 --> 00:02:55.746
The first fab alone is put at about 5,300 acre feet a year, roughly 1.7 billion gallons,

00:02:56.186 --> 00:03:01.766
about what 15,000 Phoenix households use, and Sarah Porter at Arizona State University's

00:03:01.766 --> 00:03:05.726
Kyle Center estimates about 15% or a bit more evaporates.

00:03:06.246 --> 00:03:08.806
Nearly 15 megawatts of solar sit on site.

00:03:08.806 --> 00:03:12.626
The panels doubling as covered parking for about 4,000 vehicles.

00:03:13.086 --> 00:03:18.886
The first three fabs are estimated to employ 6,000 people, up from about 3,500.

00:03:19.486 --> 00:03:23.586
Maricopa County lists the project as an active Title V air permit source.

00:03:24.126 --> 00:03:31.106
The 2025 Sustainability Report says most pollutants were cut 95% or more, and volatile organic

00:03:31.106 --> 00:03:33.786
compounds by 98.9%.

00:03:33.786 --> 00:03:39.646
TSMC says 96% of waste is recycled, and less than 1% reaches a landfill.

00:03:40.569 --> 00:03:45.789
Google has announced a data center plan near Chateau-Rue, France, and Data Center Dynamics

00:03:45.789 --> 00:03:49.109
reports a connection request for a second data center in that area.

00:03:49.649 --> 00:03:55.369
The headline says 1.2 gigawatts, and the story address reads 12 gigawatts, so the unit

00:03:55.369 --> 00:03:57.189
in what is visible does not settle.

00:03:57.769 --> 00:04:04.129
Chuck Schumer, Zaubao reports by way of Reuters, wrote on X on Tuesday, November 24th, that

00:04:04.129 --> 00:04:08.629
The Jensen Huang shipping highly advanced chips to China was akin to selling rocket engines

00:04:08.629 --> 00:04:13.629
